<article class="env-lemma" id="0B80">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B80">Lemma <span data-tag="0B80">70.17.3</span>.</a> Let $f: X \to S$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated morphism from an algebraic space to a scheme $S$. If for every $x \in |X|$ with image $s = f(x) \in S$ the algebraic space $X \times _ S \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}_{S,s})$ is a scheme, then $X$ is a scheme. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $x \in |X|$. It suffices to find an open neighbourhood $U$ of $s = f(x)$ such that $X \times _ S U$ is a scheme. As $X \times _ S \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}_{S, s})$ is a scheme, then, since $\mathcal{O}_{S, s} = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \mathcal{O}_ S(U)$ where the colimit is over affine open neighbourhoods of $s$ in $S$ we see that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  X \times _ S \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}_{S, s}) = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits X \times _ S U  \]
</div>
    <p>
       By Lemma <a href="/tag/07SR" data-tag="07SR">70.5.11</a> we see that $X \times _ S U$ is a scheme for some $U$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>